# Canonical-URL handling for https://gro-better.com/compliance
# (https, apex/non-www, no trailing slash) — design-spec.md 1.1/1.4. The
# "zero broken-link" quality bar is measured against that exact URL, so
# every variant below must resolve to it rather than silently serving
# content at multiple effective URLs.
#
# Assumption this rewrite depends on: gro-better.com's document root is
# dedicated to this app (assets/ and api/ live at domain root; see
# public/assets/form.js's API_URL comment). "/compliance" is treated as a
# virtual, rewritten path to index.html — NOT a real filesystem
# directory — specifically so Apache's own automatic "add a trailing
# slash to directory requests" behavior (mod_dir) never fires and fights
# with the chosen no-trailing-slash canonical form.
#
# NOT YET VERIFIED against the real lima-city vhost (credentials pending
# as of 2026-09-07 — see CLAUDE.md decision log). Whoever completes the
# Day 2 deploy must confirm:
#   1. mod_rewrite is enabled on the lima-city account and AllowOverride
#      permits these rules to take effect at all (see phase-0/Dockerfile
#      for the equivalent local-dev config),
#   2. the assumption above still holds — i.e. nothing else needs to live
#      at this domain's root; if gro-better.com hosts other content too,
#      these rules and the absolute asset/API paths need revisiting,
#   3. there isn't a conflicting rewrite/redirect already configured at
#      the host level (some managed-hosting control panels inject their
#      own https/www redirects, which can loop against these rules).

RewriteEngine On

# Force https
RewriteCond %{HTTPS} off
RewriteRule ^ https://%{HTTP_HOST}%{REQUEST_URI} [L,R=301]

# Force apex (non-www)
RewriteCond %{HTTP_HOST} ^www\.(.+)$ [NC]
RewriteRule ^ https://%1%{REQUEST_URI} [L,R=301]

# /compliance/ (trailing slash) -> /compliance (canonical, no slash)
RewriteRule ^compliance/$ /compliance [R=301,L]

# Serve index.html for /compliance without changing the visible URL and
# without an actual directory lookup (see assumption above).
RewriteRule ^compliance$ /index.html [L]
